# 10. USB Transport Strategy

## MVP transport

Use:

ADB port forwarding.

Conceptually:

```text
Mac
 |
 | ADB
 |
 +---- USB ----+
              |
              Android
              |
              One+Connect service
```

The Mac creates a TCP-like logical channel through ADB.

Example conceptual connection:

```text
Mac localhost:27183
        ↓
ADB forward
        ↓
Android localhost:27183
        ↓
One+Connect service
```

This lets us build the application protocol using a reliable byte stream without immediately writing a custom USB driver.

---

# 11. Production Transport

After the MVP works, evaluate moving from ADB to a dedicated USB transport.

Android supports USB accessory/host modes through its USB APIs, including direct communication using USB endpoints.

Potential production architecture:

```text
Mac USB host
      ↓
One+Connect USB protocol
      ↓
Android USB accessory
      ↓
One+Connect
```

However, this should be treated as a separate engineering phase.

ADB is not a bad choice for V1 because your intended product already requires USB debugging.

