# 80. The Most Important Architectural Rule

The application should never know that the display is "the OnePlus Pad Go 2" deep inside the rendering system.

Instead:

```text
DisplayBackend
     ↓
OnePlusPadBackend
```

Later:

```text
DisplayBackend
 ├── OnePlusPad
 ├── AndroidTablet
 ├── iPad
 └── OtherDevice
```

Likewise:

```text
Transport
 ├── ADBTransport
 └── USBAccessoryTransport
```

And:

```text
Input
 ├── CGEventInput
 └── HIDInput
```

This means we can replace individual pieces without rewriting the entire application.

